# LINE ENDINGS FOR THE FILES THAT ARE RUN ON LINUX.
#
# The repository is developed on Windows, where Git's autocrlf hands the
# working tree CRLF. That is fine for TypeScript, but the deployment files are
# read by a Linux container and by GitHub Actions: a Dockerfile or a shell
# script with CR at the end of every line is the classic "$'\r': command not
# found" failure, and it only shows up in CI.
#
# Committing these as LF costs nothing on Windows (editors and Git handle it)
# and takes that whole class of failure off the table. After adding this file,
# `git add --renormalize .` rewrites what is already committed.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# The supplied art, audio and the player rig: never touched by line-ending
# conversion, which would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp3 binary
*.fbx binary
*.zip binary
